#EXTM3U
# DotBox - test playlist
#
# Free, publicly available streams to try an M3U player such as DotBox: a live channel and
# three open movies. DotBox itself ships no content; this list only points to streams their
# owners publish openly. Every address was checked on 2026-11-17 (a real video segment or the
# start of the file was downloaded); test streams move, so check them again before use.
#
# Licences (each checked at its source on 2026-11-17):
# - The live channel is a public test stream run by iReplay.tv (ireplay.tv) for testing
#   players. No licence is published for the stream itself: use it for testing only, as it is
#   offered. What it plays are the Blender Foundation's open movies, under CC BY (below).
# - Sintel, Tears of Steel and Elephants Dream are open movies of the Blender Foundation,
#   released under Creative Commons Attribution licences (CC BY). Their posters, from
#   Wikimedia Commons, are under the licences noted beside each movie. CC BY allows sharing,
#   commercial use included, with the credit given below.

# iReplay.tv test channel: the Blender open movies played one after the other, 24/7, as a live
# stream (HLS with fragmented MP4 pieces and its sound in a list of its own, 270p to 1080p, a
# discontinuity between movies). Public test stream, no published licence.
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Tests - Live",iReplay - Blender movies (live)
https://ireplay.tv/test/blender.m3u8

# The same channel, a single 1080p rendition.
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Tests - Live",iReplay - Blender movies 1080p (live)
https://ireplay.tv/test/hd_blender.m3u8

